# Commits `git blame` should look through: whole-repository mechanical changes that say nothing about
# who wrote a line or why.
#
# GitHub reads this file by name. For a local checkout, once:
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# The first entry will be the commit that applies the Biome formatter to the whole tree
# (`npm run format`). It is made once, in a commit of its own, after the branches that touch source
# have merged, and its full 40-character hash goes below on its own line with a comment saying what it
# was. Nothing is listed yet.
